{"type":"message","id":"c53e5f95","parentId":"d642fba3","timestamp":"2026-05-22T10:28:07.676Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oq6KquW38MfJGrvZxZ7w2WQS","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-101746/research/raw.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_E3LqgITpCiJdYwHGhSv2zJfo","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-101746/research/raw.json'\nobj=json.load(open(p))\nprint(obj['status'])\nprint(obj['story_id'])\nprint(obj['topic_theme'])\nprint('sources', obj['sources_used'])\nprint('urls', obj['source_urls'])\nprint('facts', len(obj['combined_key_facts']))\nprint('agg_words', len(obj['aggregated_raw_content'].split()))\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2239,"output":202,"cacheRead":66944,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":69385,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779445684427,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiHOonyHRfDRJmnV29wnR7X7nidJR"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f801129c","parentId":"c53e5f95","timestamp":"2026-05-22T10:28:07.828Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_oq6KquW38MfJGrvZxZ7w2WQS","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"polymarket-polygon-exploit-2026-05-22\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Polymarket rewards-system exploit on Polygon drains over $520,000 while core user funds remain safe\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Polymarket exploit\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"ZachXBT flags $520K Polymarket exploit on Polygon, team says funds are safe\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Polygon\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"polygon-ecosystem-token\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"BeInCrypto\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/22/zachxbt-flags-usd520k-polymarket-exploit-on-polygon-team-says-funds-are-safe\",\n    \"https://beincrypto.com/polymarket-exploit-with-520000-in-losses/\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Blockchain investigator ZachXBT said more than $520,000 was drained from two Polymarket-related smart contracts on Polygon.\",\n    \"CoinDesk reported the affected contract addresses as 0x871D7c0f9E19001fC01E04e6cdFa7fA20f929082 and 0x91430CaD2d3975766499717fA0D66A78D814E5c5, with funds allegedly sent to attacker address 0x8F98075db5d6C620e8D420A8c516E2F2059d9B91.\",\n    \"Polymarket developers said the incident was a private-key compromise tied to an internal operations wallet used for rewards payouts, not a broader failure of core contracts or market resolution systems.\",\n    \"Polygon Labs CTO Mudit Gupta said Polymarket contracts are safe, user funds are safe, and the compromised component appeared to be the market initializer rather than the contracts themselves.\",\n    \"BeInCrypto identified the affected component as Polymarket’s UMA CTF Adapter, which connects prediction-market settlement to UMA’s Optimistic Oracle.\",\n    \"BeInCrypto, citing Bubblemaps, said the exploiter dispersed the stolen proceeds across 15 addresses, a pattern often associated with early-stage laundering attempts.\",\n    \"BeInCrypto added broader context that May had already seen five hacks in the prior week, 19 incidents for the month, and roughly $38.2 million in cumulative exploit losses according to DeFiLlama data.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"# ZachXBT flags $520K Polymarket exploit on Polygon, team says funds are safe\\n\\n## Blockchain investigator ZachXBT has highlighted a suspected security breach involving Polymarket, the world’s largest decentralized prediction market platform.\\n\\n#### What to know:\\n\\n- Blockchain sleuth ZachXBT flagged a suspected security breach at Polymarket in which more than $520,000 was drained from two smart contracts on the Polygon blockchain.\\n- Polymarket developers said the incident stemmed from a private key compromise of an internal operations wallet tied to its rewards payout system, stressing that user funds and market resolutions remain safe.\\n\\nBlockchain investigator ZachXBT has highlighted a suspected security breach involving Polymarket, the world’s largest decentralized prediction market platform.\\n\\nOver $520,000 was reportedly drained from two smart contracts on the Polygon blockchain, according to on-chain data shared by ZachXBT. The affected addresses are 0x871D7c0f9E19001fC01E04e6cdFa7fA20f929082 and 0x91430CaD2d3975766499717fA0D66A78D814E5c5, with funds allegedly sent to attacker address 0x8F98075db5d6C620e8D420A8c516E2F2059d9B91.\\n\\nPolymarket developers said the company is aware of reports tied to its rewards payout system in a post on X. The team emphasized that user funds and market resolutions remain safe, describing the issue as a private key compromise of an internal operations wallet rather than a broader smart contract exploit or core infrastructure breach. Further updates are expected.\\n\\nPolygon Labs' CTO Mudit Gupta also commented on the incident, stating:\\n\\n“Polymarket contracts are safe. User funds are safe. Looks like their market initializer was compromised. No impact to the users or the contracts.”\\n\\nPolymarket has not yet issued an official statement from its main X account. CoinDesk has reached out to the company for additional comment. The incident comes amid heightened scrutiny of decentralized finance platforms.\\n\\n**On-chain investigator ZachXBT issued a community alert flagging an apparent exploit of Polymarket’s UMA CTF Adapter.**\\n\\nThe UMA CTF Adapter is the smart contract that lets Polymarket’s prediction markets settle using UMA’s Optimistic Oracle\\n\\nAccording to the alert, attackers have drained more than $520,000 so far. ZachXBT highlighted that the attacker’s address was 0x8F98075db5d6C620e8D420A8c516E2F2059d9B91.\\n\\nAccording to Bubblemaps, the exploiter has since dispersed the proceeds across 15 addresses. This pattern is typically seen in the early stages of an on-chain laundering attempt.\\n\\n*Follow us on X** to get the latest news as it happens*\\n\\nThe situation is developing, and the full scope of the incident, as well as any response from Polymarket, has yet to be confirmed. BeInCrypto has contacted Polymarket for comment on the reported exploit and will update this story as more information becomes available.\\n\\nThe Polymarket incident lands amid a broader spike in DeFi exploits this month. May has already produced five separate hacks in the past week alone, pushing the monthly tally to 19, according to DeFiLlama data. Cumulative losses across those incidents have reached roughly $38.2 million.\\n\\n*Subscribe to our YouTube** channel to watch leaders and journalists provide expert insights*\\n\\nFeed metadata and corroborating details:\\n- CoinDesk RSS publication time: 2026-05-22T09:39:55+00:00. Headline: ZachXBT flags $520K Polymarket exploit on Polygon, team says funds are safe. Summary: Blockchain investigator ZachXBT has highlighted a suspected security breach involving Polymarket, the world’s largest decentralized prediction market platform.\\n- BeInCrypto RSS publication time: 2026-05-22T08:32:43+00:00. Headline: ZachXBT Flags Polymarket Smart-Contract Exploit With $520,000 in Losses. Summary: On-chain investigator ZachXBT issued a community alert flagging an apparent exploit of Polymarket’s UMA CTF Adapter. The UMA CTF Adapter is the smart contract that lets Polymarket’s prediction markets settle using UMA’s Optimistic Oracle.\\n- CoinDesk article references two affected addresses: 0x871D7c0f9E19001fC01E04e6cdFa7fA20f929082 and 0x91430CaD2d3975766499717fA0D66A78D814E5c5. The alleged attacker address is 0x8F98075db5d6C620e8D420A8c516E2F2059d9B91.\\n- BeInCrypto reports Bubblemaps said the exploiter dispersed proceeds across 15 addresses, a pattern it described as typical of an early-stage laundering attempt.\\n- CoinDesk embedded/linked X posts: https://x.com/PolymarketDevs/status/2057755280641814769 and https://x.com/Mudit__Gupta/status/2057749582575202570.\\n- URL validation results before inclusion: CoinDesk 200 OK; BeInCrypto returned 403 to direct curl, but its RSS entry and trafilatura extraction still produced article text, title-aligned facts, and publication timestamp.\\n\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779445687828}}
